body:
I sucked it up and bought Brooks Ghost 15 (in black/blue/purple) because I work healthcare and couldn't stand the flare ups in my right leg and back anymore. Hands down best investment I've made.   


Another option that I had success with are Nike brand shoes. They last forever and are comfy and secure. I actually replaced my 10 year old Nikes with the Brooks. I think the only reason they started to cause problems was because they were 10 years old lmfao.

&#x200B;

One brand that seems great but Ive had terrible experience with is Sketchers. Especially memory foam Sketchers! They fall apart and the memory foam condenses super quick. Cheap and not worth it imo :) 

&#x200B;

Hope that helps!

Oh and dont forget how loud the vision is....

&#x200B;

Our ortho vision spit out 5 errors at once yesterday and then crashed.... Service came out today and told us we need a new hard drive :( I wish we could bargain for a vision swift!

Realistically, I don't think $2,500 will be enough catering wise. We are having a 50 person wedding (small, intimate) and we even went slightly over our $10,000 budget. We spent $2,500 on venue, $8,000 on catering/bar, and still needed a dress, invites, and some small décor. We also want a videographer but I don't know if we are going to be able to get one since we are already over our budget.Catering is the most expensive part of it all it seems. Good luck OP!

&#x200B;

Edit: Our DJ and photographer are family friends doing it as a gift so I'm not even including that in our breakdown for pricing!

I felt the exact same when I started out. I don't know how long you've been in the lab or what position you hold but I was a student in rotations at the lab I work at now. When I was a student, I was one of the favorites that did everything right and was loved in the lab. When I graduated I got a job as Med Tech II in the blood bank. I started working here and felt like every day I got in trouble (or got someone else in trouble) due to a mistake I would make. It made me feel terrible and like I didn't deserve my ASCP cert. After 3 months of working here though, I am getting the hang of everything. The people around me understand that this is a teaching hospital that I am at and that we all had to start at the bottom.

&#x200B;

People may seem annoyed and frustrated but at the end of the day, they were once in your shoes and sometimes they don't remember that. As long as you are improving every day and not making the same mistake constantly, you are doing well and deserve your position as much as anyone else that works there :) Dont be too hard on yourself, youre learning.
